{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function QueryErrorResetBoundary(props: QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps): Element;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx#L160","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx:160"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"suspense"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" in your queries, you need a way to let queries know that you want to\ntry again when re-rendering after some error occurred. With the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryErrorResetBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" component you can\nreset any query errors within the boundaries of the component."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" to render."}]},{"type":"html","value":"<a id=\"props-properties\"></a>"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"props-properties","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" properties"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"props-property-children\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactNode"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/QueryErrorResetBoundaryFunction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryErrorResetBoundaryFunction"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Either a plain node, or a function that receives the boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue and returns a node."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Element"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":", rendered as-is, or called with the boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue\nif "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" is a function."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ErrorBoundary } from 'react-error-boundary'\nimport { QueryErrorResetBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <QueryErrorResetBoundary>\n      {({ reset }) => (\n        <ErrorBoundary\n          onReset={reset}\n          fallbackRender={({ resetErrorBoundary }) => (\n            <div>\n              There was an error!\n              <button onClick={() => resetErrorBoundary()}>Try again</button>\n            </div>\n          )}\n        >\n          <Page />\n        </ErrorBoundary>\n      )}\n    </QueryErrorResetBoundary>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"props","text":"props","level":3},{"id":"props-properties","text":"props properties","level":4},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction QueryErrorResetBoundary(props: QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps): Element;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx:160](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx#L160)\n\nWhen using `suspense` or `throwOnError` in your queries, you need a way to let queries know that you want to\ntry again when re-rendering after some error occurred. With the `QueryErrorResetBoundary` component you can\nreset any query errors within the boundaries of the component.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### props\n\n[`QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps`](../interfaces/QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps.md)\n\nThe `children` to render.\n\n<a id=\"props-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `props` properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"props-property-children\"></a> `children` | \\| `ReactNode` \\| [`QueryErrorResetBoundaryFunction`](../type-aliases/QueryErrorResetBoundaryFunction.md) | Either a plain node, or a function that receives the boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue and returns a node. |\n\n## Returns\n\n`Element`\n\nThe `children`, rendered as-is, or called with the boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue\nif `children` is a function.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { ErrorBoundary } from 'react-error-boundary'\nimport { QueryErrorResetBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <QueryErrorResetBoundary>\n      {({ reset }) => (\n        <ErrorBoundary\n          onReset={reset}\n          fallbackRender={({ resetErrorBoundary }) => (\n            <div>\n              There was an error!\n              <button onClick={() => resetErrorBoundary()}>Try again</button>\n            </div>\n          )}\n        >\n          <Page />\n        </ErrorBoundary>\n      )}\n    </QueryErrorResetBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: QueryErrorResetBoundary\ntitle: QueryErrorResetBoundary\nredirect_from:\n  - framework/react/reference/QueryErrorResetBoundary\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction QueryErrorResetBoundary(props: QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps): Element;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx:160](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/react-query/src/QueryErrorResetBoundary.tsx#L160)\n\nWhen using `suspense` or `throwOnError` in your queries, you need a way to let queries know that you want to\ntry again when re-rendering after some error occurred. With the `QueryErrorResetBoundary` component you can\nreset any query errors within the boundaries of the component.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### props\n\n[`QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps`](../interfaces/QueryErrorResetBoundaryProps.md)\n\nThe `children` to render.\n\n<a id=\"props-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `props` properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"props-property-children\"></a> `children` | \\| `ReactNode` \\| [`QueryErrorResetBoundaryFunction`](../type-aliases/QueryErrorResetBoundaryFunction.md) | Either a plain node, or a function that receives the boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue and returns a node. |\n\n## Returns\n\n`Element`\n\nThe `children`, rendered as-is, or called with the boundary's QueryErrorResetBoundaryValue\nif `children` is a function.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { ErrorBoundary } from 'react-error-boundary'\nimport { QueryErrorResetBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <QueryErrorResetBoundary>\n      {({ reset }) => (\n        <ErrorBoundary\n          onReset={reset}\n          fallbackRender={({ resetErrorBoundary }) => (\n            <div>\n              There was an error!\n              <button onClick={() => resetErrorBoundary()}>Try again</button>\n            </div>\n          )}\n        >\n          <Page />\n        </ErrorBoundary>\n      )}\n    </QueryErrorResetBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
